§ `Article 25`

@export Under Article 25(1), as a distributor, am I considered to be the provider of the high-risk AI system?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) and related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if you do not know of such a product.
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where the AI system is high-risk because of Article 6(1), does the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lay down requirements or obligations that give an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights than the requirement or obligation the question is about? Answer no if you do not know.
      `limiting the requirement or obligation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would limiting the requirement or obligation the question is about leave the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation unreduced? Answer no if you do not know.
      `the party puts its name or trademark on a high-risk AI system already placed on the market or put into service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you put your name or trademark on a high-risk AI system already placed on the market or put into service?
      `the party makes a change to the AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make a change to the AI system after your placing on the market or putting into service?
      `the change is foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment carried out by the provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the change is foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment carried out by the provider?
      `as a result of the change the compliance of the AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 is affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that as a result of the change the compliance of the AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 is affected?
      `the change results in a modification to the intended purpose for which the AI system has been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the change results in a modification to the intended purpose for which the AI system has been assessed?
      `the AI system remains a high-risk AI system pursuant to Article 6 after the change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the AI system remains a high-risk AI system pursuant to Article 6 after the change?
      `the party modifies the intended purpose of an AI system which has not been classified as high-risk and has already been placed on the market or put into service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you modify the intended purpose of an AI system which has not been classified as high-risk and has already been placed on the market or put into service?
      `the AI system concerned becomes a high-risk AI system in accordance with Article 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the AI system concerned becomes a high-risk AI system in accordance with Article 6?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under Article 25(1), as a distributor, am I considered to be the provider of the high-risk AI system` MEANS
    `Art 25(1) the party is considered to be the provider of the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` `the party`
    WHERE
        `the AI system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
        `the circumstances` MEANS `Section 3 circumstances` WITH
            `related to Section B products` IS `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
            `Section A equivalent protection` IS `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection`
            `no reduction of the overall level of protection` IS `limiting the requirement or obligation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`
        `the party` MEANS `Art 25(1) what the party has done` OF TRUE, `the party puts its name or trademark on a high-risk AI system already placed on the market or put into service`, `the party makes a change to the AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service`, `the change is foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment carried out by the provider`, `as a result of the change the compliance of the AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 is affected`, `the change results in a modification to the intended purpose for which the AI system has been assessed`, `the AI system remains a high-risk AI system pursuant to Article 6 after the change`, `the party modifies the intended purpose of an AI system which has not been classified as high-risk and has already been placed on the market or put into service`, `the AI system concerned becomes a high-risk AI system in accordance with Article 6`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat distributor from part P8 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P8 seat layer: a distributor: what the AI Office and the market surveillance authorities may do to an operator, and what an operator must do under Articles 74 to 79.
-- SEAT: a distributor
--
-- Nothing here is new law: each question calls the layer-1 function of Articles 72 to 79 (P8-art72 to P8-art79) that answers it, and the keel
-- (aia-definitions, aia-timeline, aia-core) for the role facts and the dates. Every question takes plain inputs: a yes/no, a date, a number or
-- one of the keel's own choices, each with an @desc worded for the person asking. A question answers JUST value, or NOTHING where the text does
-- not decide it (the Regulation does not apply yet on the date asked, or the text is silent); a JUST FALSE is a "no" the text itself gives.
-- Questions are grouped by Article in the order of the text; the role question and the applicability questions come first.


§ `The role the person asking holds`

-- The role, worked out by the keel's definition; the other questions of this seat assume it.
@export Under Article 74, as a distributor, am I a distributor within the meaning of Article 3(7)?
GIVEN `the party is in the supply chain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in the supply chain?
      `the party is the provider of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the provider of the AI system?
      `the party is the importer of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the importer of the AI system?
      `the party makes the AI system available on the Union market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make the AI system available on the Union market?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 74, as a distributor, am I a distributor within the meaning of Article 3(7)` IS
    `Art 3(7) the party is a distributor` `the party is in the supply chain` `the party is the provider of the AI system` `the party is the importer of the AI system` `the party makes the AI system available on the Union market`

§ `Which provisions apply on the date asked`

-- Calls the gate helper of P8-gate, which passes the group to the keel's `Art 113 the provision group applies`.
@export Under Article 72, as a distributor, does General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 72, as a distributor, does General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)

§ `Article 74: Market surveillance and control of AI systems in the Union market`
-- Arises only when a market surveillance authority acts on the AI system; the access questions arise only after its request.

-- Calls `Art 74(1)(a) the party is understood as an economic operator under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020`.
@export Under Article 74(1), as a distributor, am I understood as an economic operator under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 74(1), as a distributor, am I understood as an economic operator under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020` IS
    `Art 74(1)(a) the party is understood as an economic operator under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020` `the date asked` Distributor

§ `Article 75a: Supervisory and enforcement powers of the AI Office`
-- Arises only if the AI Office is supervising or enforcing against the operator.

-- Calls `Art 75a(1) second sentence the AI Office is authorised to fully reclaim from the relevant operator the totality of the costs of its supervision and enforcement activities`.
@export Under Article 75a(1), as a distributor, is the AI Office authorised to fully reclaim from me the totality of the costs of its supervision and enforcement activities?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the costs are costs of the supervision and enforcement activities of the AI Office with respect to instances of non-compliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the costs are costs of the supervision and enforcement activities of the AI Office with respect to instances of non-compliance?
      `the costs are reclaimed from the relevant operator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the costs are reclaimed from the relevant operator?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 75a(1), as a distributor, is the AI Office authorised to fully reclaim from me the totality of the costs of its supervision and enforcement activities` IS
    `Art 75a(1) second sentence the AI Office is authorised to fully reclaim from the relevant operator the totality of the costs of its supervision and enforcement activities` `the date asked` `the costs are costs of the supervision and enforcement activities of the AI Office with respect to instances of non-compliance` `the costs are reclaimed from the relevant operator`

-- Calls `Art 75a(2) second sentence the AI Office must notify the operator of the AI system concerned`.
@export Under Article 75a(2), as a distributor, must the AI Office notify me as the operator of the AI system concerned?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the AI Office has started an investigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the AI Office has started an investigation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 75a(2), as a distributor, must the AI Office notify me as the operator of the AI system concerned` IS
    `Art 75a(2) second sentence the AI Office must notify the operator of the AI system concerned` `the date asked` `the AI Office has started an investigation`

-- Calls `Art 75a(3) first subparagraph the AI Office may exercise the powers listed in Article 14(4), points (a), (b) and (c) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 and Article 74(12) and (13) by simple request or by decision`.
@export Under Article 75a(3), as a distributor, may the AI Office exercise the powers listed in Article 14(4), points (a), (b) and (c) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 and Article 74(12) and (13) by simple request or by decision?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 75a(3), as a distributor, may the AI Office exercise the powers listed in Article 14(4), points (a), (b) and (c) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 and Article 74(12) and (13) by simple request or by decision` IS
    `Art 75a(3) first subparagraph the AI Office may exercise the powers listed in Article 14(4), points (a), (b) and (c) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 and Article 74(12) and (13) by simple request or by decision` `the date asked`

-- Calls `Art 75a(4) first sentence the AI Office may conduct all necessary remote or on-site inspections`.
@export Under Article 75a(4), as a distributor, may the AI Office conduct all necessary remote or on-site inspections?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the inspection is necessary to carry out the tasks assigned to the AI Office under this Section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the inspection is necessary to carry out the tasks assigned to the AI Office under this Section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 75a(4), as a distributor, may the AI Office conduct all necessary remote or on-site inspections` IS
    `Art 75a(4) first sentence the AI Office may conduct all necessary remote or on-site inspections` `the date asked` `the inspection is necessary to carry out the tasks assigned to the AI Office under this Section`

-- Calls `Art 75a(6)(a) the AI Office may order operators to provide access to, and explanations relating to, their AI systems`.
@export Under Article 75a(6), as a distributor, may the AI Office order me to provide access to, and explanations relating to, my AI system?
